    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **285 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`.\n- Records the authenticated user (`SecurityContextHolder\u2026getAuthentication().getName()`), the new owner's id, and membership number.\n- Reads the owner via `@Val Owner` (the same instance mutated/saved earlier in the pipeline).\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a new `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so the owner's id is already assigned by the time it logs. It carries the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbours.\n\nThe message emitted, e.g. `Owner created by user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`, satisfies the cp19 acceptance test which asserts the AUDIT logger captured both the user and the owner id.",
